Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `text`, which this function owns
  --> returned_string_view_slice_rejects_local_owner.jet:5:10
    |
  5 |     text.slice(0..<3)
    |          ^^^^^
 Why: `text` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
